WEBVTT

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:09.518
A report pipeline describes work, while its result

00:00:09.518 --> 00:00:10.456
stores values.

00:00:10.456 --> 00:00:13.874
We will build a pending stream, collect its report,

00:00:13.874 --> 00:00:15.617
and make an editable copy.

00:00:36.237 --> 00:00:39.750
Lazy evaluation means processing waits for a terminal

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:40.413
operation.

00:00:40.413 --> 00:00:43.793
Pending describes how to add a label to each source

00:00:43.793 --> 00:00:44.125
item.

00:00:44.125 --> 00:00:46.776
Creating it does not collect the report.

00:00:46.776 --> 00:00:50.289
This ArrayList source is late bound: its contents are

00:00:50.289 --> 00:00:53.007
observed when terminal processing begins.

00:00:53.007 --> 00:00:56.520
Notice that kit is added before toList, not while the

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.912
stream is processing.

00:00:58.213 --> 00:01:00.938
The report is an unmodifiable result list.

00:01:00.938 --> 00:01:04.183
Its entries cannot be added, removed, or replaced.

00:01:04.183 --> 00:01:07.687
The ArrayList constructor makes a collection copy with

00:01:07.687 --> 00:01:09.374
a separate list structure.

00:01:09.374 --> 00:01:12.813
This is a shallow copy: both lists initially hold the

00:01:12.813 --> 00:01:14.306
same String references.

00:01:14.306 --> 00:01:16.577
Strings cannot be changed in place.

00:01:16.577 --> 00:01:19.756
A stream is single use, so the final count uses a

00:01:19.756 --> 00:01:21.379
fresh stream from source.

00:01:21.379 --> 00:01:24.688
Count returns long, Java's wider whole-number type.

00:01:24.773 --> 00:01:26.844
Predict all four output lines.

00:01:26.844 --> 00:01:29.882
Track when kit enters source, when report is

00:01:29.882 --> 00:01:32.989
collected, and which list receives Item: pen.

00:01:32.989 --> 00:01:33.748
Pause here.

00:01:38.523 --> 00:01:41.916
The report contains two items because kit was added

00:01:41.916 --> 00:01:43.114
before collection.

00:01:43.114 --> 00:01:46.307
Adding Item: pen changes only the editable copy.

00:01:46.307 --> 00:01:49.700
The original result stays at two, the copy grows to

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:52.428
three, and the fresh source count is two.

00:01:52.428 --> 00:01:55.954
You can read the stored report again, but pending has

00:01:55.954 --> 00:01:59.148
already been consumed by its terminal operation.

00:01:59.478 --> 00:02:02.445
Move the kit addition to just after the report is

00:02:02.445 --> 00:02:03.051
collected.

00:02:03.051 --> 00:02:05.412
Predict all four counts before running.

00:02:05.412 --> 00:02:08.500
Which counts should change, and what does that tell

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.528
you about the report's relationship to its source?
